<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ title }}</title>
<style>
:root {
  --bg: #fcfcfb; --surface: #ffffff; --text: #0b0b0b; --muted: #52514e; --line: #e4e3df;
  --accent: #2a78d6; --warn-bg: #fff4e0; --warn-text: #7a4b00; --ok-bg: #e8f3ec; --bad-bg: #fde8e8;
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root { --bg: #1a1a19; --surface: #242423; --text: #ffffff; --muted: #c3c2b7; --line: #3a3a38;
          --accent: #3987e5; --warn-bg: #3a2c10; --warn-text: #f5c56b; --ok-bg: #1d3326; --bad-bg: #3d1f1f; }
  svg { background: #ffffff; border-radius: 6px; }
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
body { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text);
       font: 15px/1.55 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif; }
main { max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 16px 64px; }
h1 { font-size: 1.7rem; margin: 0 0 4px; }
h2 { font-size: 1.3rem; margin: 40px 0 8px; padding-top: 8px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
h3 { font-size: 1rem; margin: 20px 0 8px; }
.meta, .muted { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; }
.disclaimer { background: var(--warn-bg); color: var(--warn-text); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; margin: 16px 0; }
.tiles { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(170px, 1fr)); gap: 12px; margin: 16px 0; }
.tile { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 12px 14px; }
.tile .label { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; }
.tile .value { font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 600; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; background: var(--surface); }
table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-size: 0.9rem; }
th, td { padding: 8px 10px; text-align: right; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); white-space: nowrap; }
th:first-child, td:first-child { text-align: left; }
th { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; }
tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
.ci { display: block; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.78rem; }
.badge { display: inline-block; font-size: 0.72rem; padding: 1px 7px; border-radius: 999px; margin-left: 6px;
         border: 1px solid currentColor; color: var(--muted); }
.badge.small { color: var(--warn-text); background: var(--warn-bg); border-color: transparent; }
.charts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 460px), 1fr)); gap: 16px; margin-top: 16px; }
svg { max-width: 100%; height: auto; }
.charts svg { width: 100%; }
figure { margin: 0; min-width: 0; }
.charts > * { min-width: 0; }
.findings li { margin: 8px 0; }
.findings .ids { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.78rem; }
.rejected { background: var(--bad-bg); border-radius: 8px; padding: 10px 14px; margin-top: 12px; font-size: 0.9rem; }
.verified { background: var(--ok-bg); border-radius: 8px; padding: 8px 14px; font-size: 0.85rem; }
dl { display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 6px 16px; }
dt { color: var(--muted); }
dd { margin: 0; }
details summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--accent); }
.caught { margin-top: 12px; font-size: 0.9rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<header>
  <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
  <div class="meta">{{ dataset }} · generated {{ generated }} · EquityPanel {{ version }}</div>
  <p class="disclaimer"><strong>Auditing aid for research and education, not a clinical
  tool.</strong> This report measures how a model's performance differs between groups in the data
  it was given; its numbers describe that dataset, not any individual. It is not medical advice,
  has not been clinically validated, and must not be used to make or influence decisions about
  individual patients. It does not certify a model as fair, safe or compliant.</p>
  {% if tiny_groups %}
  <p class="disclaimer"><strong>Very small groups:</strong> {{ tiny_groups | join("; ") }}. Each has
  fewer than 11 patients, or fewer than 11 readmitted or not-readmitted patients, so its numbers
  can reveal individual outcomes. If this report was built from real patient data, do not share
  it outside your organization.</p>
  {% endif %}
</header>

<section>
  <h2>Key numbers</h2>
  <div class="tiles">
  {% for label, value in key_numbers %}
    <div class="tile"><div class="label">{{ label }}</div><div class="value">{{ value }}</div></div>
  {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% if small_groups %}
  <p class="muted">Small groups (fewer than 30 readmitted or not-readmitted patients; treat their
  numbers as uncertain): {{ small_groups | join(", ") }}.</p>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Summary</h2>
  {% if summary is none %}
  <p class="muted">Summary not generated. The optional plain-English summary needs an Anthropic
  API key; every number below is computed without it.</p>
  {% elif summary.error %}
  <p class="muted">Summary not available: {{ summary.error }}.</p>
  {% else %}
  <p class="verified"><strong>AI-generated summary.</strong> An AI model wrote these findings from
  the report's aggregate numbers only; it saw no individual patient records. Software confirmed
  that each number it cites matches a value in the tables below. The wording, comparisons and
  conclusions were not checked and may be wrong or misleading, and no person has reviewed this
  summary. Rely on the tables, and have a qualified person review before acting on anything
  here.</p>
  <ul class="findings">
  {% for f in summary.findings %}
    <li>{{ f.text }} <span class="ids">[{{ f.fact_ids | join(", ") }}]</span></li>
  {% endfor %}
  </ul>
  {% if summary.rejected_final %}
  <div class="rejected"><strong>{{ summary.rejected_final | length }} finding(s) rejected</strong> by
  the number check and not shown above:
    <ul>
    {% for r in summary.rejected_final %}<li>{{ r.reason }}: “{{ r.text }}”</li>{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  {% if summary.rejected_earlier %}
  <details class="caught">
    <summary>The number check caught {{ summary.rejected_earlier | length }} finding(s) in an
    earlier draft; the model was told why and rewrote them</summary>
    <ul>
    {% for r in summary.rejected_earlier %}<li>Attempt {{ r.attempt }}: {{ r.reason }}: “{{ r.text }}”</li>{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </details>
  {% endif %}
  {% endif %}
</section>

{% for s in sections %}
<section id="{{ s.col }}">
  <h2>By {{ s.title | lower }}</h2>
  <p class="muted">Each cell shows the estimate and its 95% confidence interval. Gaps are
  differences from the reference group, <strong>{{ s.reference }}</strong> (the largest); gaps in
  rates are in percentage points (pts).</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Group</th><th>Patients</th><th>Readmitted</th>
      {% for h in headers %}<th>{{ h }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for r in s.rows %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ r.group }}{% if r.is_reference %}<span class="badge">reference</span>{% endif %}{% if r.small %}<span class="badge small">small group</span>{% endif %}</td>
        <td>{{ r.n }}</td><td>{{ r.n_pos }}</td>
        {% for c in r.cells %}<td>{{ c.value }}<span class="ci">{{ c.ci }}</span></td>{% endfor %}
      </tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
  <h3>Gaps vs {{ s.reference }}</h3>
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Group</th>{% for h in headers %}<th>{{ h }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for r in s.rows if not r.is_reference %}
      <tr><td>{{ r.group }}{% if r.small %}<span class="badge small">small group</span>{% endif %}</td>
        {% for g in r.gaps %}<td>{{ g }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
  <div class="charts">
  {% for chart in s.charts %}<figure style="margin:0">{{ chart | safe }}</figure>{% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>
{% endfor %}

{% if egfr %}
<section id="egfr">
  <h2>eGFR: race-based (2009) vs race-free (2021) kidney formula</h2>
  <p class="disclaimer"><strong>{{ egfr.label }}</strong> The direction of the change matches
  published real-world studies; the sizes do not estimate real prevalence.</p>
  <p>Until 2021 the standard kidney-function formula (CKD-EPI 2009) multiplied a Black patient's
  result by 1.159, making their kidneys look healthier. Counts below are patients below each
  clinical line under 2009 → under 2021. The equations are computed only to count how this
  cohort moves; they are not for estimating any individual's kidney function.</p>
  <figure style="margin:0">{{ egfr.chart | safe }}</figure>
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Group</th><th>Patients</th><th>Worse stage</th><th>Better stage</th>
      <th>eGFR &lt; 60 (CKD line)</th><th>eGFR &lt; 30 (common referral line)</th><th>eGFR ≤ 20 (transplant waiting-time line)</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for r in egfr.rows %}
      <tr><td>{{ r.group }}{% if r.kind == "race" %}<span class="badge">race</span>{% endif %}{% if r.small %}<span class="badge small">small group</span>{% endif %}</td>
        <td>{{ r.n }}</td><td>{{ r.lower }}</td><td>{{ r.higher }}</td>
        {% for l in r.lines %}<td>{{ l }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}

<section id="methods">
  <h2>Methods and limitations</h2>
  <dl>
    <dt>Flagging rule</dt><dd>A patient is flagged when their risk score is at or above the
    threshold{% if model_info %} ({{ "%.3f" | format(model_info.threshold) }}, set on training
    patients to flag about 10%){% endif %}.</dd>
    <dt>Confidence intervals</dt><dd>95% stratified bootstrap{% if methods.n_boot %}
    ({{ methods.n_boot }} resamples, seed {{ methods.seed }}){% endif %}: patients are resampled
    within each group and outcome.</dd>
    <dt>Reference group</dt><dd>The largest group in each column; gaps are group minus reference.</dd>
    <dt>Small groups</dt><dd>Flagged, not dropped, when they have fewer than 30 readmitted or
    fewer than 30 not-readmitted patients.</dd>
    {% if summary and not summary.error %}
    <dt>Summary model</dt><dd>{{ summary.model }} via the Anthropic API, given only aggregate
    numbers ({{ summary.attempts }} attempt(s)). Small-cell suppression before sending:
    {% if summary.min_cell %}on (groups or counts of 1 to {{ summary.min_cell - 1 }} removed){% else %}off (public data){% endif %}.</dd>
    {% endif %}
    <dt>Metrics</dt><dd>AUC: how well scores rank readmitted above not-readmitted patients
    (0.5 = chance). Brier: average squared error of the risk (lower is better). O/E: observed ÷
    expected readmissions (1 = calibrated; above 1 = risk underestimated). FPR: flagged but not
    readmitted. FNR: readmitted but not flagged. PPV: flagged patients who were readmitted.</dd>
    <dt>What this cannot tell you</dt><dd>Why a gap exists, whether the labels themselves are
    biased (who gets readmitted depends on access to care), or how the model performs on other
    hospitals' patients. Race, sex and age are audit variables, not model inputs.</dd>
  </dl>
  {% if model_info and model_info.top_weights %}
  <details>
    <summary>Model inputs with the largest weights</summary>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table>
      <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Weight</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{% for w in model_info.top_weights %}<tr><td>{{ w.feature }}</td><td>{{ "%+.3f" | format(w.weight) }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
    </table></div>
  </details>
  {% endif %}
</section>
<footer class="muted" style="margin-top:48px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:12px;font-size:0.8rem">
  {% for credit in data_credits %}<p>{{ credit }}</p>{% endfor %}
  <p>Generated by EquityPanel {{ version }}, an independent open-source project provided "as is"
  under the MIT License, without warranty of any kind. Not affiliated with or endorsed by any
  organization named in this report. If this report was built from real patient data, store and
  share it only under your organization's data-governance rules, and never publish it, including
  on GitHub Pages.</p>
  {% if footer_note %}<p>{{ footer_note }}</p>{% endif %}
</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
